        "body": "## Problems confirmed from the latest runtime log\n\n1. Bot 3 reaches category and Samsung brand correctly, but every `CATALOG_SCAN` fails while resolving the exact `Galaxy S25` model. The runtime reports 24-28 visible model rows, no exact label, then retries the catalog job.\n2. The dedicated Market Stats observer reaches the Vinted e-mail form and submits it, but authentication does not complete. Because login happens before the target loop, that single failure currently prevents all 76 market-stat targets from being scanned.\n3. Independent `NEGOTIATION_CHECK` jobs already continue correctly after a catalog failure; that scheduler isolation is preserved.\n\n## S25 model-selection fix\n\n- use plain-string `hasText(model)` only to narrow the current Vinted model list to likely rows; no unsupported regexp flags are involved\n- keep final selection fail-closed: a row is accepted only after the exact requested model label is recovered\n- inspect the selectable row plus visible `label`, `span`, and `p` descendants; fall back to `textContent`, `aria-label`, and `title` when row `innerText()` is empty\n- preserve exact rejection of sibling variants such as `Galaxy S25 Edge`, `Galaxy S25 Ultra`, `Galaxy S25 FE`, and `Galaxy S25+`\n- improve failure diagnostics with text-narrowing counts and actual partial labels\n- avoid repeatedly interrogating every Samsung model row, which made the nominal 10-second model wait take far longer in production\n\n## Market Stats observer fix\n\nMarket Stats is a read-only collector: it only visits the public catalog, applies filters, scans listing ids and records observations in our backend. It never submits offers or negotiation actions.\n\n- authenticated observer login is still preferred\n- if observer login fails for a non-interruption reason, collection continues in anonymous read-only catalog mode instead of dropping the whole daily pass\n- after login failure the page is explicitly returned to the catalog before target scanning starts\n- an anonymous context is never saved over the observer's stored session\n- login failure remains clearly logged, including full details at DEBUG\n- if anonymous Vinted access itself cannot scan a target, the existing per-model failure/retry handling still reports that transparently\n\n## Safety / unchanged behavior\n\nNo negotiation, quota, real-submit, scheduler cadence, listing-target matching or pricing semantics are changed. A catalog failure still cannot delay the bot's independent negotiation checks.",
